# fixedbugs, defect 396, lane b13-land-buf, 2026-10-07: panel 196's R4, an
# extent the declaration understates. `digest32` writes 32 bytes and the
# binding says 16, the binding's word being wrong about C. The buffer ends at
# a page nothing may touch, so C stops on its seventeenth byte and the
# runtime names the call and the parameter, exit 134, where the canary the
# sitting built first was silent under `--sanitize` and the bare buffer wrote
# over its neighbour.
extern "fixedbugs-396-buffers.h"
    function digest32(@md: [u8] counted_by 16 lent) -> i32

function main()
    md: [u8] @ []
    print("before")
    print(digest32(@md))
    print("not reached ", md.len())
